> dat = data.frame(A = c(1.56, 10, 15, 20, 30, 40, 45, 50, 1200))
> dat$B = pincus(dat$A)
>
> print(dat)
>
> ifelse is a vectorized version of if() {} else {} so it tests each value.
> With this, you get:
>
> A B
> 1 1.56 2
> 2 10.00 2
> 3 15.00 2
> 4 20.00 2
> 5 30.00 4
> 6 35.00 6
> 7 40.00 6
> 8 45.00 8
> 9 50.00 8
> 10 1200.00 238
>
